# PROD ONLY. Narrows the public API host to what callers outside the platform need. Not part of the dev stack: dev
# has no file in /etc/caddy/api.d, so the `import` in the Caddyfile adds nothing and dev routing stays as it was.
# compose.prod.yaml mounts this file at /etc/caddy/api.d/restricted.caddy. It is spliced into the API host's site
# block before the host's own `handle` blocks, so the 404 below wins.
#
# The Workspace and the portal reach the API over the internal network (API_INTERNAL_URL=http://api:3001), never
# through this host, so they are not affected.
#
# Allowed (a caller outside the platform needs these):
#   /v1/hooks/postal     Postal bounce webhook
#   /v1/hooks/zitadel    ZITADEL actions webhook
#   /v1/public/*         anonymous logo paths
#   /v1/files/*          signed file links in emails
#   /health/live         external uptime probe (/health/ready stays internal)
# Everything else answers 404. /metrics is already refused by the Caddyfile.
#
# Caddy matches on the cleaned path (dot segments and doubled slashes resolved), so /v1/public/../me is judged as
# /v1/me and refused.
@api_denied not path /v1/hooks/postal /v1/hooks/zitadel /v1/public/* /v1/files/* /health/live
handle @api_denied {
	respond 404
}
